{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A wrapped quotation can expose private holdout observations to the reviewer and then the implementer, defeating the holdout boundary in realistic free-text reports."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Short criterion IDs or generic evidence can cause unrelated report lines to be withheld, depriving the reviewer of information needed for a decision."}]}